    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-startup",
      "text": "01Keep startup coordination separate from healthy warm-up\nSTATEDStartup\n\nSupply registry grace, heartbeat, authorization polling, readiness polling and old-process termination through policy. Remove t",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-shutdown",
      "text": "02Keep distinct stop, idle and acknowledgement clocks\nSTATEDShutdown\n\nRequire shutdown policy for idle lifetime, controller stop, signal waits and drain acknowledgements. Preserve the half-window boun",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-diagnostics",
      "text": "03Policy owns both diagnostic storage limits\nSTATEDDiagnostics\n\nLogger rotation, backup count and queue capacity use diagnostics policy. Disconnected operation traces use its retention and capacity, k",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-framing",
      "text": "04Carry chunk and frame caps through each validator\nSTATEDTransport\n\nTransport, binary codec, file reader and both worker-message endpoints use supplied caps. JSON and execution-control limits stay se",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-output",
      "text": "05One output slice governs capture and retention\nSTATEDOutput\n\nRemove local inline, record, per-result and aggregate limits. Pass the same output slice into command capture and completion spooling, in",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-purpose",
      "text": "06Choose a response deadline by composition purpose\nSTATEDTransport\n\nStatus aggregation explicitly selects status-observer (100 ms); ordinary lifecycle and execution-status requests retain 250 ms. Adm",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-resources",
      "text": "07Use snapshot memory values without a second derivation\nSTATEDResources\n\nDelete the CLI resource-policy class and memory-cap input. The snapshot now supplies RSS thresholds, reported hard cap, worker",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-child-retry",
      "text": "08Count startup retries for explicit child failure\nSTATEDStartup\n\nReplace the fixed second launch with a loop bounded by childFailureRetryLimit. Only child-exit or lost-warm-up errors consume it; test",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-delivery",
      "text": "09Give execute reattachment and result fetch separate budgets\nSTATEDTransport\n\nReplace the fixed reattachment wrapper and fetch boolean with independent numeric counters. Every execute attempt owns a ",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-adapters",
      "text": "10Move legacy test knobs into seven test-only adapters\nSTATEDTests\n\nTests import adapter subclasses or a resource adapter that builds validated policy. Runtime constructors require policy; test clocks",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-error-provenance",
      "text": "11Let a later completion failure become the reported error\nUNEXPLAINEDTransport\n\nThe new reattachment loop propagates the current completion failure when its budget is exhausted. A failure to obtain t",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-test-shape",
      "text": "12Adjust small test policies and their storage paths\nUNEXPLAINEDTests\n\nValid policies require positive chunks ≤ inline ≤ result ≤ aggregate. Tests replace inline=0 and rescale chunk/inline values; ada",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-removed-tests",
      "text": "—Remove the CLI resource-derivation test block\nUNEXPLAINEDTests\n\nThe deleted block covers five memory sizes, constraint selection and the 250 ms constant. Central policy tests already cover related de",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-test-contract",
      "text": "—Use policy-based expectations and cast new fixtures\nUNEXPLAINEDTests\n\nSpool/e2e expectations now read policy defaults instead of retired constants. Three added policy-consumer cases cast through unkn",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "id": "row-guardrail",
      "text": "—Enforce retirement with a production-source string scan\nSTATEDTests\n\nExtend the package meta-test to reject old constant names, optional threshold seams and local policy reconstruction identifiers. T",
      "href": null,
      "visible": true
    },
